From: Pixel AOSP maintainers <pixel-aosp@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 01:20:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add a narrow Pixel eUICC Gservices flags provider

Pixel's proprietary eUICC firmware helper observes and reads the Gservices
authority during Application startup. Pristine AOSP deliberately has no
Google Services Framework, while adevtool extracts the six device-specific
flags needed by that helper into system_ext.

Add a standalone provider module for Pixel device products. It defines the
privileged read permission expected by the stock app, exposes only the pinned
read-only flag file, and rejects callers other than the exact installed
system/privileged eUICC package. The module is not part of any generic AOSP
product and must be selected explicitly by a device product.

This is a project-authored AOSP 17 integration fix.
License: Apache-2.0 (platform/frameworks/base)
---
 .../Android.bp                                     |  15 ++
 .../AndroidManifest.xml                            |  27 +++
 .../gservicesflags/GservicesFlagsProvider.java     | 199 +++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 241 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/Android.bp
 create mode 100644 packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/AndroidManifest.xml
 create mode 100644 packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/src/org/pixelaosp/gservicesflags/GservicesFlagsProvider.java

diff --git a/packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/Android.bp b/packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/Android.bp
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/Android.bp
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+package {
+    default_applicable_licenses: ["frameworks_base_license"],
+}
+
+android_app {
+    name: "PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider",
+    srcs: ["src/**/*.java"],
+    platform_apis: true,
+    certificate: "platform",
+    privileged: true,
+    system_ext_specific: true,
+    optimize: {
+        enabled: false,
+    },
+}
diff --git a/packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/AndroidManifest.xml b/packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/AndroidManifest.xml
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/AndroidManifest.xml
@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
+<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
+    package="org.pixelaosp.gservicesflags">
+
+    <permission
+        android:name="com.google.android.providers.gsf.permission.READ_GSERVICES"
+        android:protectionLevel="signature|privileged" />
+
+    <queries>
+        <package android:name="com.google.euiccpixel" />
+    </queries>
+
+    <application
+        android:allowBackup="false"
+        android:defaultToDeviceProtectedStorage="true"
+        android:directBootAware="true"
+        android:hasCode="true"
+        android:label="Pixel AOSP Gservices flags provider">
+        <provider
+            android:name=".GservicesFlagsProvider"
+            android:authorities="com.google.android.gsf.gservices"
+            android:directBootAware="true"
+            android:exported="true"
+            android:grantUriPermissions="false"
+            android:permission="com.google.android.providers.gsf.permission.READ_GSERVICES" />
+    </application>
+</manifest>
diff --git a/packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/src/org/pixelaosp/gservicesflags/GservicesFlagsProvider.java b/packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/src/org/pixelaosp/gservicesflags/GservicesFlagsProvider.java
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/packages/PixelAospGservicesFlagsProvider/src/org/pixelaosp/gservicesflags/GservicesFlagsProvider.java
@@ -0,0 +1,199 @@
